# esp32-c5-wroom-1-n8r8 -- ESP32-C5-WROOM-1-N8R8, the DELIVERABLE C5 target.
#
# B397: this file did not exist, and its absence shipped a broken package.  `deliverable` lives in
# w3_pio/boards.json and the ship-list lives here, and nothing tied the two together -- so when the
# C5 was switched to deliverable the only manifests in the tree were the PER-UNIT bench ones
# (-00, -01), which are not deliverable.  `w3_assemble` therefore produced no data_staged for this
# env, `w3_make_release_one` warned "release ships WITHOUT a data/ filesystem image" and carried on,
# and the customer package went out with no embedded filesystem: the board boots with none of its
# runtime .scm files present.  Measured on the 2026-09-14 03:08 release sweep, where it was the only
# one of twelve deliverable envs missing a manifest.
#
# WHY THIS IS NOT A COPY OF THE -00 BENCH MANIFEST.  It is that list MINUS two lines:
#     optional: runtime-defaults/Settings-local.scm -> Settings-local.scm
#     optional: runtime-defaults/net-test-ca.pem    -> net-test-ca.pem
# Those stage the BENCH WiFi credentials and the test CA.  Every other deliverable manifest still
# carries them and relies on w3_make_release_one deleting them again by name afterwards ([B398],
# [B399]) -- a denylist that has already been found leaking twice.  A manifest that never stages
# them cannot be un-stripped by a future edit to the stripper, so this one does not.
# The per-unit -00/-01 manifests KEEP those lines: a bench board legitimately needs both.
#
# Everything below is the -00 ship-list verbatim.  Keep the three in sync where they overlap --
# if you add a module to -00 and -01, add it here too.

core/setup.scm
core/Compiler.scm
core/Lobs.scm
core/Behaviors.scm
core/Terminal.scm
file: boards/pins/esp32-c5-wroom-1-n8r8.scm -> Pins.scm
core/Timers.scm
core/ESP32.scm
core/CommonIO.scm
core/Sonar.scm
core/I2C.scm
core/Wire.scm
core/PCA9685.scm
core/PCF8574.scm
core/LCD1602.scm
core/Buzzer.scm
core/WiFi.scm
core/WS2812.scm
core/LightSensor.scm
core/array.scm

# R5RS/R7RS overrides
rxrs/rxrs.scm
rxrs/rxrs_cxr.scm
rxrs/rxrs_exceptions.scm
rxrs/rxrs_continuations.scm
rxrs/rxrs_promises.scm
rxrs/rxrs_quasiquote.scm
rxrs/rxrs_syntax.scm
rxrs/rxrs_library.scm
rxrs/rxrs_srfi.scm

# Serial file+command tunnel: resident LLIP receiver -- needed AT BOOT to accept pushed files,
# which is how the ll_tests suite reaches an embedded FS at all (w3_ai_scripts/llip_test_runner.py).
features/llip-serial.scm
features/csv.scm
features/dh_groups.scm
features/rsa.scm
features/Neopixel.scm

tools/test-framework.scm
tools/llip-server.scm

# Runtime defaults
runtime-defaults/Settings.scm
runtime-defaults/Settings-Lamb.scm

# Test suite -- the same lean embedded pattern as the S3 manifests: bench + the NCG fusion probe
# ride the FS image; the correctness tiers are pushed incrementally over LLIP.
file: tests/ll_tests/bench-runner.scm     -> ll_tests/bench-runner.scm
file: tests/ll_tests/benchmarks.scm       -> ll_tests/benchmarks.scm
file: tests/ll_tests/bignum-hw-probe.scm  -> ll_tests/bignum-hw-probe.scm
file: tests/ll_tests/ncg-fusion-probe.scm -> ll_tests/ncg-fusion-probe.scm
file: tests/ll_tests/gc-pause-bench.scm   -> ll_tests/gc-pause-bench.scm
file: tests/ll_tests/pause_bench.scm      -> ll_tests/pause_bench.scm
